  {
   "type": "trace",
   "title": "Land",
   "structure": "geo",
   "instruction": "Trace the mountain and the land.",
   "note": {
    "text": "The geosphere is Earth's rock, soil and sand, from mountains to the deep rock below.",
    "remember": "Geosphere = rock and soil."
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "trace",
   "title": "Ocean",
   "structure": "hydro",
   "instruction": "Trace the wavy ocean.",
   "note": {
    "text": "The hydrosphere is all of Earth's water and ice: oceans, rivers, lakes, glaciers, and water underground.",
    "remember": "Hydrosphere = water and ice."
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "trace",
   "title": "Cloud",
   "structure": "atmo",
   "instruction": "Trace the cloud in the sky.",
   "note": {
    "text": "The atmosphere is the layer of air around Earth. Clouds, wind and weather happen in it.",
    "remember": "Atmosphere = air."
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "trace",
   "title": "Tree",
   "structure": "tree",
   "instruction": "Trace the tree.",
   "note": {
    "text": "The biosphere is every living thing on Earth, including plants, animals and people.",
    "remember": "Biosphere = living things."
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "trace",
   "title": "Fish",
   "structure": "fish",
   "instruction": "Trace the fish in the ocean.",
   "note": {
    "text": "Living things are found in every other sphere: on land, in the water, and flying through the air."
